        "id": "record_graph_edit_events",
        "instruction": "Edit src/amendments.rs, src/harness_evolution.rs, and src/supervise.rs so every accepted human split, reroute, cancel, dependency edit, and autonomous grow/repair/differentiate graph mutation appends a compact learning event through project_file APIs. Capture the verified graph_before_hash before mutation; controlled action type with target and created_nodes; bounded trigger; actor identity; timestamp; and eventual_effect success/rework_reduced, initially unknown where necessary and updated when downstream evidence arrives. Ensure rejected/no-op edits do not claim success, child graph hashes remain valid, and created/cancelled/superseded nodes get appropriate structural and controlled outcome fields. Add tests for all four human-edit forms, autonomous edits, event ordering, before-hash accuracy, eventual-effect update, and no-op rejection. Do not edit runtime lifecycle files, persistence schema, Swift, sync, or dist-* files.\n\nREPAIR: a previous attempt did NOT succeed at `record_graph_edit_events` (it failed verification, or the agent got stuck / timed out). Read any error output and fix the implementation and tests so the whole suite passes. If the earlier approach was slow, blocking, interactive, or hung, SIMPLIFY it: avoid long-running or interactive operations and produce a minimal, correct version quickly.",
        "kind": "container",
        "memory_scopes": [
          "work:goal",
          "workspace:root"
