        "instruction": "Edit src/execute.rs, src/orchestrate.rs, src/run_control.rs, and src/checkpoint.rs to call the central project_file learning mutation APIs at dependency readiness, checkout/start, success, execution error, verification failure, timeout, retry/reopen, cancellation/stale release, resume, and human completion. Record executor agent/model/version-or-config-hash from real agent configuration, increment attempt_count only for actual starts, attach controlled outcomes/failure codes, verification type/passed/compact evidence_refs, actual elapsed agent time and actual cost only when measured, and artifact production/consumption IDs where runtime facts exist. Map errors deterministically to requested failure codes without arbitrary self-evaluation; preserve previous attempts on retry. Extend module tests for retries, tool failure, timeout, failed verification, cancellation, stale release/resume, artifact lineage, human intervention, and monotonic timestamps. Do not edit graph-edit producers, persistence schema, sync, Swift, or dist-* files.\n\nREPAIR: a previous attempt did NOT succeed at `record_graph_edit_events` (it failed verification, or the agent got stuck / timed out). Read any error output and fix the implementation and tests so the whole suite passes. If the earlier approach was slow, blocking, interactive, or hung, SIMPLIFY it: avoid long-running or interactive operations and produce a minimal, correct version quickly.",
